      "kind": "Economics",
      "text": [
        {
          "m": "s",
          "sid": "p86762f969a56.1",
          "c": [
            "Khatri printers knew their clients through hereditary relationships and bartered their dyed cloth directly with them for milk, animals and ",
            {
              "m": "cite",
              "key": "rm:p86762f969a56.1",
              "g": [
                "g14",
                "g13"
              ],
              "c": [
                "grain."
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " ",
        {
          "m": "s",
          "sid": "p86762f969a56.2",
          "c": [
            "Khatri printers of Kutch have almost stopped printing ajrakh for Maldharis, who buy cheaper screen-printed cloth in chemical dyes, mostly from Pakistan and from ",
            {
              "m": "cite",
              "key": "rm:p86762f969a56.2",
              "g": [
                "g2",
                "g14",
                "g6"
              ],
              "c": [
                "Khavda."
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " ",
        {
          "m": "s",
          "sid": "p86762f969a56.3",
          "c": [
            "In 2014 Abduljabbar M. Khatri's workshop made 70,000 m of running cotton yardage for Fabindia, one of his largest clients with ",
            {
              "m": "cite",
              "key": "rm:p86762f969a56.3",
              "g": [
                "g11"
              ],
              "c": [
                "Maiwa."
              ]
            }
